    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener>
                    <dateline><date when="1947-04-10">April 10, 1947</date></dateline><salute>Dear
                            <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Mr.
                        Tillich</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>We were delighted to receive your letter of <date when="1947-04-02">April 2,
                        1947</date>,<note type="ea">Liegt nicht vor.</note> and to learn that you
                    agree with us on the advisability to plan your SYSTEMATIC THEOLOGY as a
                    two-volume work approximately 250,000 words in total length.</p>
                <p>On this basis, we hope to present the project to our Publications Committee in
                    the near future with the suggestion to authorize a definite commitment on our
                    part.</p>
                <p>The organization of this work is of course entirely in your hands and I am
                    retracting my recent remark that the two volumes might be made independent of
                    each other. What I meant to say was that perhaps the work could be so organized
                    that Volume I might be published before Volume II. You will, of course, rely
                    entirely on your own judgment in this matter.</p>
                <p>I hope the above will allow you to plan your work for the balance of this year. I
                    hope to be able, within a month or so, to inform you of a favorable decision of
                    our Publication Committee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>Very sincerely yours,</salute>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rend="hand"><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__2057" type="person">Fred
                                Wieck</rs></hi><lb/><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__2057" type="person"
                            >Fred Wieck</rs><lb/>Associate Editor</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
